    id: "article-1769022733567",
    title: "Canggu, Bali - Guide to Long Term Villa Rental and Living",
    slug: "canggu-bali-guide-to-long-term-villa-rental-and-living",
    category: "areas",
    content: "<p>Canggu is one of the most popular destinations in Bali for long‑term villa rentals and digital nomads. It blends beach culture, green landscapes, trendy cafés, and a global community. Canggu’s popularity continues to grow as a lifestyle hub, attracting people who want to stay months or years on the island.</p><hr><h2 class=\"heading\"><strong>Overview</strong></h2><p>Located on Bali’s southwest coast between Seminyak and Pererenan, Canggu is known for its surf beaches, rice fields, cafés, and creative scene. The neighborhood keeps expanding, covering areas such as Berawa, Batu Bolong, Nelayan, and inland rice paddies near Seseh and Munggu.</p><p>Canggu is a balanced mix of:</p><ul><li><p><strong>Beach lifestyle</strong></p></li><li><p><strong>Surf culture</strong></p></li><li><p><strong>Creative cafés and restaurants</strong></p></li><li><p><strong>Work‑friendly spots for remote professionals</strong></p></li><li><p><strong>Green inland areas with rice field views</strong></p></li></ul><p>This combination makes Canggu attractive for long‑term rentals, especially for those who want both lifestyle and community.</p><hr><h2 class=\"heading\"><strong>Who Lives in Canggu</strong></h2><p>Canggu attracts a diverse community:</p><ul><li><p><strong>Digital nomads</strong> who work from cafés and coworking spaces</p></li><li><p><strong>Surfers</strong> and beach lovers drawn to consistent breaks like Echo Beach</p></li><li><p><strong>Young expats and couples</strong> seeking a casual yet social lifestyle</p></li><li><p><strong>Families and longer‑term residents</strong> who appreciate the balance of quiet and social life</p></li></ul><p>The area is popular with people in their 20s–40s, especially professionals who enjoy flexibility, outdoor life, and international communities.</p><hr><h2 class=\"heading\"><strong>Why People Love Canggu</strong></h2><p>Canggu is loved for its relaxed yet lively vibe. You can surf in the morning, work from a café by noon, meet friends for brunch, or watch the sunset by the beach. The café culture here is strong, with places like <strong>Crate Café, Shady Shack, Milk &amp; Madu, Motion Café</strong>, and more offering a range of food, drinks, and work‑friendly environments.</p><p>The area also shows Bali’s evolving culture — rice paddies remain visible near café spots, and this mix of nature with modern living creates a unique tropical lifestyle.</p><hr><h2 class=\"heading\"><strong>Main Attractions and Lifestyle</strong></h2><p><strong>Beaches and Surf</strong></p><ul><li><p><strong>Echo Beach</strong> — great surf and sunset spot with a laid‑back vibe</p></li><li><p><strong>Batu Bolong Beach</strong> — popular social area with beachside cafés and bars</p></li><li><p><strong>Berawa Beach</strong> — relaxed surf and chill spots</p></li></ul><p><strong>Café and Dining Scene</strong><br>Canggu’s culinary scene ranges from healthy brunch spots and vegan cafés to stylish sunset bars:</p><ul><li><p><strong>Crate Café</strong></p></li><li><p><strong>Shady Shack</strong></p></li><li><p><strong>Milk &amp; Madu</strong></p></li><li><p><strong>Milu by Nook</strong> (near rice fields)</p></li></ul><p><strong>Rice Field Views and Nature</strong><br>Canggu isn’t just beaches. Near Seseh and Munggu you’ll find traditional rice fields and scenic countryside spots perfect for walks, yoga classes with views, or calm afternoons outside the busy beach scene.</p><hr><h2 class=\"heading\"><strong>Supermarkets and Daily Essentials</strong></h2><p>For long‑term living, Canggu offers a good range of practical amenities:</p><ul><li><p><strong>Pepito Market</strong> — quality grocery and international products</p></li><li><p><strong>Bali Buda</strong> — organic groceries</p></li><li><p><strong>Local minimarts</strong> — for everyday essentials and quick purchases</p></li></ul><p>These make daily life comfortable, reducing the need for frequent trips to larger towns.</p><hr><h2 class=\"heading\"><strong>Community and Social Life</strong></h2><p>Canggu has an active social scene with meetups, wellness events, yoga classes, and creative workshops. Many people here stay because they find:</p><ul><li><p>a supportive expat community</p></li><li><p>frequent social activities</p></li><li><p>places where you can both work and relax</p></li></ul><p>This makes it particularly attractive for long‑term residents.</p><hr><h2 class=\"heading\"><strong>Things to Consider Before Renting Long Term</strong></h2><p>While Canggu has a strong appeal, consider:</p><ul><li><p><strong>Traffic congestion</strong> at peak hours, especially around Batu Bolong and Berawa</p></li><li><p><strong>Development pressure</strong>, with new construction visible in many areas</p></li><li><p><strong>Higher rental prices</strong> compared to quieter inland or northern Bali zones</p></li></ul><p>Despite these, the lifestyle advantages often outweigh the inconveniences for many long‑term renters.</p><hr><h2 class=\"heading\"><strong>Summary</strong></h2><p>Canggu offers one of the most complete long‑term living experiences in Bali. It combines:</p><ul><li><p>beach life</p></li><li><p>creative café culture</p></li><li><p>surf and outdoor activities</p></li><li><p>approachable daily amenities</p></li></ul><p>It is ideal for individuals, couples, remote workers, and even families who want a dynamic, community‑oriented lifestyle on the island.</p>",
