    id: "article-1769023752075",
    title: "Bukit, Bali - Ocean View Villas, Surf Lifestyle & Long-Term Living",
    slug: "bukit-bali-ocean-view-villas-surf-lifestyle-long-term-living",
    category: "areas",
    content: "<p>The Bukit Peninsula is the southernmost part of Bali, famous for dramatic cliffs, white-sand beaches, world-class surf spots, and private villas overlooking the ocean. This area is a top choice for those looking for <strong>long-term villa rentals in Bali</strong> with space, privacy, and a relaxed lifestyle.</p><p>Bukit offers a quieter, more refined alternative to crowded areas like Canggu or Seminyak.</p><hr><h2 class=\"heading\">Where Is Bukit Located?</h2><p>Bukit Peninsula is located in the <strong>south of Bali</strong> and includes areas such as:</p><ul><li><p>Uluwatu</p></li><li><p>Pecatu</p></li><li><p>Bingin</p></li><li><p>Padang Padang</p></li><li><p>Balangan</p></li><li><p>Parts of Jimbaran</p></li></ul><p>Ngurah Rai International Airport is <strong>30–50 minutes away</strong>, depending on traffic and exact location.</p><hr><h2 class=\"heading\">Atmosphere &amp; Lifestyle</h2><p>Living in Bukit means:</p><ul><li><p>open spaces and low-density development</p></li><li><p>ocean views and cliffside sunsets</p></li><li><p>surf-oriented lifestyle</p></li><li><p>quiet roads and less traffic</p></li><li><p>a strong wellness and nature vibe</p></li></ul><p>It’s a place for people who prefer <strong>calm, space, and nature over nightlife</strong>.</p><hr><h2 class=\"heading\">Who Lives in Bukit?</h2><h3 class=\"heading\">Main residents:</h3><ul><li><p>expats aged 30–55</p></li><li><p>surfers and remote workers</p></li><li><p>families with children</p></li><li><p>entrepreneurs and long-term Bali residents</p></li></ul><h3 class=\"heading\">Lifestyle interests:</h3><ul><li><p>surfing</p></li><li><p>yoga &amp; wellness</p></li><li><p>remote work</p></li><li><p>private villa living</p></li></ul><p>Bukit attracts people who plan to <strong>stay long-term</strong>, not just visit for a few days.</p><hr><h2 class=\"heading\">Tourist Profile &amp; Age Groups</h2><ul><li><p><strong>25–35</strong> — surfers, digital nomads, couples</p></li><li><p><strong>35–50</strong> — families, long-term renters</p></li><li><p><strong>50+</strong> — relaxed lifestyle, ocean-view villas</p></li></ul><p>Bukit is not a party destination — it’s a <strong>long-stay residential area</strong>.</p><hr><h2 class=\"heading\">Long-Term Villa Rental in Bukit</h2><h3 class=\"heading\">Typical villas include:</h3><ul><li><p>1–4 bedrooms</p></li><li><p>private swimming pool</p></li><li><p>terrace or garden</p></li><li><p>parking area</p></li><li><p>ocean or sunset views</p></li></ul><h3 class=\"heading\">Long-term rental prices (approximate):</h3><ul><li><p>1 bedroom: <strong>IDR 18–25 million / month</strong></p></li><li><p>2 bedrooms: <strong>IDR 25–40 million / month</strong></p></li><li><p>3–4 bedrooms: <strong>IDR 45 million+ / month</strong></p></li></ul><p>Bukit offers excellent <strong>value for space, privacy, and views</strong>.</p><hr><h2 class=\"heading\">Beaches &amp; Attractions</h2><h3 class=\"heading\">Popular spots:</h3><ul><li><p>Uluwatu Temple</p></li><li><p>Padang Padang Beach</p></li><li><p>Bingin Beach</p></li><li><p>Balangan Beach</p></li><li><p>Dreamland Beach</p></li><li><p>Karma Beach</p></li></ul><p>Many beaches are accessed by stairs, keeping them natural and uncrowded.</p><hr><h2 class=\"heading\">Cafés &amp; Restaurants</h2><p>Bukit’s café scene is growing fast:</p><ul><li><p><strong>Single Fin</strong> — iconic ocean-view venue</p></li><li><p><strong>Drifter Café</strong> — surf café and lifestyle store</p></li><li><p><strong>Nourish Café</strong> — healthy food</p></li><li><p><strong>The Cashew Tree</strong> — brunch &amp; relaxed dining</p></li><li><p><strong>Ulu Garden</strong> — sunset drinks and music</p></li></ul><p>The focus here is quality, views, and atmosphere.</p><hr><h2 class=\"heading\">Supermarkets &amp; Daily Shopping</h2><ul><li><p>Nirmala Supermarket</p></li><li><p>Pepito</p></li><li><p>Bintang Supermarket (larger locations nearby)</p></li><li><p>Local minimarkets</p></li></ul><p>For major shopping trips, many residents drive to Kerobokan or Seminyak.</p><hr><h2 class=\"heading\">Who Is Bukit Ideal For?</h2><p>Bukit is perfect if you:</p><ul><li><p>want a <strong>long-term villa rental in Bali</strong></p></li><li><p>value peace and privacy</p></li><li><p>work remotely</p></li><li><p>love surfing or ocean views</p></li><li><p>prefer spacious living</p></li></ul><p>If nightlife and constant activity are important, Canggu or Seminyak may suit you better.</p><hr><h2 class=\"heading\">Conclusion</h2><p>The Bukit Peninsula is one of the best areas in Bali for <strong>long-term villa rentals</strong>, offering space, tranquility, and stunning nature. It’s ideal for families, surfers, and anyone seeking a calm, high-quality lifestyle close to the ocean.</p>",
