    id: "article-1769025597201",
    title: "Kerobokan, Bali - Strategic Long-Term Living Between Canggu and Seminyak",
    slug: "kerobokan-bali-strategic-long-term-living-between-canggu-and-seminyak",
    category: "areas",
    content: "<p>Kerobokan is one of the most practical areas in Bali for long-term living. Located between Canggu and Seminyak, it offers a balance of accessibility, residential atmosphere, and more reasonable rental prices compared to the most popular tourist zones.</p><p>Kerobokan is often chosen by people who want to stay close to everything without living in the center of heavy tourist activity.</p><hr><h2 class=\"heading\">Area Overview</h2><p>Kerobokan is situated in South Bali, directly east of Seminyak and south of Canggu. The area is mostly residential, with a mix of villas, local neighborhoods, and small commercial zones.</p><p>It does not have a single center and is spread across several sub-areas, which makes location choice important when renting long term.</p><hr><h2 class=\"heading\">Who Lives in Kerobokan</h2><p>Kerobokan attracts a wide range of long-term residents:</p><p>• expats working in Canggu or Seminyak<br>• remote workers<br>• families with children<br>• entrepreneurs and small business owners</p><p>The area has a more stable long-term population compared to Canggu, with fewer short-term tourists.</p><hr><h2 class=\"heading\">Age Groups and Lifestyle</h2><p>• 30–45 years old — remote workers and couples<br>• 35–55 years old — families and long-term residents<br>• Fewer party-oriented visitors</p><p>Kerobokan suits people who want <strong>a calmer home base</strong> while staying close to social and business hubs.</p><hr><h2 class=\"heading\">Why People Choose Kerobokan</h2><p>Kerobokan is popular for several reasons:</p><p>• central location<br>• easier traffic compared to Canggu<br>• more residential and quiet streets<br>• better value for long-term rentals<br>• proximity to international schools</p><p>It offers convenience without the constant tourist pressure.</p><hr><h2 class=\"heading\">Housing and Long-Term Rental Market</h2><p>Typical rental options include:</p><p>• private villas<br>• small villa complexes<br>• townhouses<br>• guesthouse-style homes</p><p>Prices are generally lower than in central Canggu and Seminyak, especially for larger villas.</p><p>Kerobokan is often chosen for <strong>yearly rentals</strong>.</p><hr><h2 class=\"heading\">Cafés, Restaurants, and Daily Life</h2><p>Kerobokan has enough cafés and restaurants for daily needs, though most residents also visit nearby areas.</p><p>Local life includes:<br>• neighborhood cafés<br>• small restaurants<br>• fitness studios<br>• yoga centers</p><p>For trendier dining, people usually go to Seminyak or Canggu.</p><hr><h2 class=\"heading\">Supermarkets and Infrastructure</h2><p>Kerobokan is strong in terms of infrastructure.</p><p>Main options include:<br>• Pepito Market<br>• Bintang Supermarket<br>• CocoMart<br>• local minimarkets</p><p>Healthcare, gyms, and service providers are easily accessible.</p><hr><h2 class=\"heading\">Schools and Family Facilities</h2><p>Kerobokan is a popular choice for families due to proximity to schools and kindergartens.</p><p>Several international and private schools are located within a short driving distance, making daily routines manageable.</p><hr><h2 class=\"heading\">Transportation and Accessibility</h2><p>Kerobokan connects easily to:<br>• Seminyak<br>• Canggu<br>• Denpasar<br>• Umalas</p><p>Roads are generally wider than in Canggu, though traffic still exists during peak hours.</p><hr><h2 class=\"heading\">Things to Consider Before Renting</h2><p>Some aspects to keep in mind:</p><p>• not walkable in most areas<br>• noise near main roads<br>• ongoing construction in some neighborhoods<br>• location within Kerobokan matters a lot</p><p>Careful villa selection is important for long-term comfort.</p><hr><h2 class=\"heading\">Atmosphere and Community</h2><p>Kerobokan has a residential, grounded feel. The community is more stable and less transient than in tourist-heavy areas.</p><p>It is a popular choice for people who plan to stay in Bali for several years.</p><hr><h2 class=\"heading\">Summary</h2><p>Kerobokan is ideal for long-term living if you want:</p><p>• a strategic location<br>• reasonable rental prices<br>• access to Canggu and Seminyak<br>• residential atmosphere<br>• family-friendly environment</p><p>It is one of the most balanced areas in South Bali for long-term villa rental.</p>",
